WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
A seismograph needle twitches.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.980
A magnitude six earthquake.

3
00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.270
Years later, another trace.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.440
This one is magnitude eight.

5
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:12.000
Eight is only a third more than six.

6
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:14.650
So is the second wave a third bigger?

7
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.850
Twice as big?

8
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.000
How many times larger is
its measured amplitude?

9
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.680
In this mission, you'll meet logarithms.

10
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:26.780
A logarithm is an index: log
base ten undoes ten to the power.

11
00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.200
On a base ten log scale, each
step of one is a factor of ten.

12
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.970
And you'll see that the earthquake magnitude
scale is exactly this kind of scale.

13
00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: decide how much bigger a
magnitude eight earthquake is than a magnitude

14
00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:41.720
six.
